{"content":[{"c":["PASEAH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Eshton’s son, the brother of Beth-rapha and a descendant of Kelub from Judah’s tribe. Paseah was mentioned as one of the men of Recah (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.12","r":"1Chr.4.12","rawR":"1Chr.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.12","value":"1Chr.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Ancestor of a family of temple servants who returned to Palestine with Zerubbabel after the Babylonian captivity (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.49","r":"Ezra.2.49","rawR":"Ezra.2.49","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.49","value":"Ezra.2.49"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:49"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.51","r":"Neh.7.51","rawR":"Neh.7.51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.51","value":"Neh.7.51"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:51"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Joiada’s father. Joiada, along with Meshullam, repaired the Old Gate of Jerusalem under Nehemiah’s direction during the postexilic period (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.6","r":"Neh.3.6","rawR":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.6","value":"Neh.3.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Paseah","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.12","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.12","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.12"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:49","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.49","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.49","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.49"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:51","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.51","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.51","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.51"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.6","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.6","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6d1bbb221e9a527776c5ce30717229f90e4ceaab09ec53fcac98e2feb1dc09e2","sourceItemName":"Paseah","sourceItemOrder":54,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Paseah","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Paseah","title":"Paseah","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}